WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:05.263
A soft brush strokes your forearm.

2
00:00:06.163 --> 00:00:08.263
Does some nerve fibre care how fast it moves?

3
00:00:09.317 --> 00:00:11.577
Mouse genetics cannot be done in people.

4
00:00:11.837 --> 00:00:16.297
So human touch classes rest on another method, microneurography.

5
00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:21.987
A fine tungsten electrode goes through the skin into a nerve, in a conscious person.

6
00:00:22.827 --> 00:00:24.447
It records single afferents.

7
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:30.190
Recordings from the hand sorted human afferents into four classes, by firing.

8
00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.370
The ending is never seen.

9
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.650
Hairy skin adds another class.

10
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:40.090
Slow, unmyelinated afferents that respond to gentle deformation.

11
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:46.560
These are the C-tactile afferents, physiologically similar to mouse C-LTMRs.

12
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.900
The brush strokes from very slow to fast.

13
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.100
Which speed drives a C-tactile afferent hardest?

14
00:00:59.183 --> 00:01:05.983
Not the fastest. C-tactile firing rises, then falls: an inverted U. It peaks in the

15
00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:06.983
slow-stroke range.

16
00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:10.623
Pleasantness ratings correlated with that firing.

17
00:01:11.803 --> 00:01:14.343
Fast myelinated Aβ afferents behaved differently.

18
00:01:15.283 --> 00:01:17.003
Their firing kept rising with speed.

19
00:01:18.017 --> 00:01:22.757
Reviews conclude that these afferents support gentle, affective touch, the social

20
00:01:22.757 --> 00:01:23.757
side of touch.

21
00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:27.007
But not every affective touch relies on them.

22
00:01:27.827 --> 00:01:29.647
And affective touch need not be pleasant.

23
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.300
The human C-tactile ending is still unknown.

24
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:37.380
The mouse hair map cannot be transplanted onto human hair.

25
00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:39.893
So the idea carries over.

26
00:01:40.813 --> 00:01:43.553
Each class is most sensitive to its own part of a touch.

27
00:01:44.413 --> 00:01:46.153
The nervous system reads the pattern.
